## ADR-005: Protected Fields in Firestore Rules

**Status:** Active

**Decision:** Firestore security rules define protected field lists for
inventory, delivery workflows, rental workflows, patient equipment, and
patient lifecycle. Client-side updates cannot modify these fields.

**Context:** Stock fields (`quantityOnHand`, `available`, etc.) and workflow
fields (`status`, `completedAt`, etc.) must only be modified by Cloud
Functions to prevent race conditions and unauthorized state changes.

**Consequences:**
- Client-side creates must have safe stock defaults (all zeros)
- Client-side updates cannot change protected fields
- Cloud Functions (`movementService.ts`) are the only path to modify stock
- Rules are complex (723 lines) and require careful maintenance

